[Music]  this morning a special edition of the  dish from the super bowl city of Atlanta  in 2017 eater named B's cracklin  barbecue as Atlanta's restaurant of the  year saying it's a must visit for the  city's barbecue lovers Dana Jacobson had  a chance to talk with owner Brian Furman  a South Carolina native whose shaking up  the barbecue scene in the South's  biggest city Dana yabbies cracklin  barbecue guys is about a 20-minute drive  from where I am here in downtown Atlanta  but it has become a destination for  barbecue fans from across the globe  when Brian Furman puts together his  sampler plate he knows that people may  come in for the meat but says it's the  sides that complete the dish all right  that looks good not gonna lie this is  all for me right Brian yes ma'am  B's cracklin barbecue Furman's  restaurant has been getting a lot of  buzz since opening in 2014 is this  Atlanta barbecue my barbecue I feel like  I got my own style his style is homemade  like the three cheese mac and cheese  baked beans with brisket scraps and fat  and cracklin hoecakes  and this is your special sauce yes  that's the peach mustard and homegrown  pork that he smokes in the back of the  restaurant bacon meat and hammy and  that's why the sandwich and the port  different Furman is no stranger to fire  before mastering the art of smoking meat  he worked as a welder for the company  JCB as for his current title he refrains  from the traditional label bestowed on  the kings of barbecue  I don't even label myself a pitmaster  you don't know like my grandma my  granddad my dad you never label  themselves a pitmaster okay my grandma  never label itself a chef  his grandmother also taught firm in a  thing or two about livestock  we're always eating things that farm on  the backyard and a garden I'm raising on  Felix raising on chickens so I grew up  basically made from scratch everything  food has always been kind of like my  thing but I just didn't look at it as a  business that changed when Furman who  suffers from migraines needed a spinal  tap that put him out of work for months  I got back to work I told my friend if I  walk through these doors 2015 you'd be  right to slap me he just laughed and I  was like I'm serious and June when I  signed a lease and I told her I quit my  job  open beans when you told your dad you  wanted to do barbecue he he asked you a  question that really helped shape some  of what you do uh-huh what was the  question what was gonna make me  different than everybody else  he found his answer back on the farm  heritage pigs which he rears from the  farm in Statesboro Georgia  to the table the heritage breed is a old  lining of pigs if you put these pigs in  the command system they won't they won't  live they won't work they won't walk on  concrete they stress they won't eat so  they had to live on dirt and you saw  that this was the best-tasting meat came  from these pigs yeah and then what was  the thought burden barbecue it's kind of  like cheating Fuhrman open bees cracklin  in Savannah before expanding to Atlanta  it's a family affair  his wife Nikki left her career as a  property manager and their two teenage  sons worked for him after school  but Fuhrman doesn't see bees as a  mom-and-pop shop his goal has always  been to open a new restaurant every year  the latest is in the renovated home of  the NBA's Atlanta Hawks State Farm arena  people go to business school for years  to try to figure it out and restaurants  still fail I'm laughing because to be  honest with you like business to me is  common sense either you're born with it  or you're born without it Fuhrman  credits his success to a keen instinct  years of hard work and 2013 my horoscope  was like your empire were flourished for  the next 19 years doesn't my horoscope  said and I'm like Empire I'm just maybe  with the Stars being aligned guys I got  enough barbecue for all of us but you're  not here to eat it with me so it does  not travel well I did however get  something that will of course a cocktail  glass with a Super Bowl theme and then  Michelle I know who you're rooting for  on Sunday because you're Saints aren't  in there so I got you a hat for your new  favorite team the Patriot it's not like  I haven't worn that hat before my super  cities challenge so you know thank you  so much I so appreciate that I'm gonna  have to deal with the bitterness back  here I hope Brian Foreman brings up  brings one of these next restaurant in  New York cuz that looks so good

